   "Clean build node receipts and undeclared environment/network/shell rejection. SAFE14 also denies undeclared postinstall, model/tool, compiler IR and unproven native generation/registry authority; permitted effects carry provider, scope, grant and trace, and hermetic release effects are replayable or have pinned outputs. Negative fixtures prove denial occurs before the external effect. Criterion `integration/build-input-capture`: Capture all declared external, session, configuration and script inputs affecting build outputs in reproducibility artifacts, or reject/mark nonhermetic behavior according to build policy. Accepted fixture: Capture declared external/session/configuration/script/environment/network/file inputs affecting build outputs with source and generator provenance. Negative fixture: Reject unrecorded nonhermetic influence or explicitly mark it according to the declared reproducibility policy; never silently certify hermeticity. Required evidence: build-input manifest and clean/replayed input-drift fixture; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, schema outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Source obligation `language/compiletime/preserve-phase-artifacts`: Schedule compile-time stages in the declared semantic order and prevent later stages or memoization from mutating earlier artifacts or losing original source/generated provenance. Accept: Schedule reading, namespace loading, expansion, name/type/effect analysis, profile/capability validation, constant evaluation, extension execution, revalidated typed-core lowering and target preparation in L12 order. Later stages may inspect immutable prior artifacts; normalization and memoization retain original spans and generated-origin chains. Reject: Reject an out-of-order dependency, unauthorized extension/target preparation, mutation of a prior artifact or loss of original/generated diagnostic provenance. Required outputs: Ordered compile-time event graph, immutable before/after artifact digests, authorization decisions and source/generated-origin diagnostic fixtures. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from expand/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/expand5-integrate-generated-programs, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open.",
