tracts. All source qualifications in the\nA1-A11 acceptance contract above also apply to this criterion.\n\nCriterion profile-gap/ai/profile-tool-contract (Open): Input: AI model/tool declaration, provider policy, typed arguments, caller/deployment grants, side-effect class and applicable review record. Accept: Admit and execute the declared model request through its provider; validate tool input/output schemas and side-effect/review policy before a tool action; re-enter ordinary macro/type/effect/capability/safety/package/profile checking before generated Gravity code can execute. Review approval never manufactures a missing capability. Reject: Missing provider/effect/policy, tool schema or grant; write/destructive/shell/deployment/package/secret action without applicable review; raw memory/FFI in agent logic; generated code executed before compiler validation. Required outputs: Agent/model/tool manifests, schema validation result, effect/grant/review decisions and generated-code validation/provenance record. The mixed original cost/token/call predicates require a source-specific billing-versus-removed-accounting decision; retain that Open policy outcome and all adjacent authority restrictions. Dependencies: schema, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, expand/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/expand5-integrate-generated-programs interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping ai/profile-tool-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/ai/prompt-memory-boundary (Open): Input: Prompt messages with roles/provenance and retrieved/tool/memory/model values carrying trust, taint, retention/deletion/privacy and secret policy. Accept: Preserve each source-visible role and origin; validate model out