   "Allocation, lifetime, transfer, race and foreign-failure conformance with explicit providers. Execute the [SAFE2-SAFE8 contracts](../../docs/phase-02-safety/README.md): declared allocation and cleanup failures, partial initialization cleanup, region/arena generation and borrow checks, release through the correct allocator/provider, callback lifetime/thread/reentrancy/release and foreign error/exception/promise translation. Reject retained borrows, post-reset access, missing FFI declarations, unsupported atomics and unsynchronized mutable access; validate immutable sharing, lock cleanup, actor/channel transfer and declared backpressure/cancellation. Inspect actual checks and audit records, with no hidden GC or host-thread fallback. . R3/R5/R6/R10: allocation/deallocation/provider manifests, no-allocation and region/arena escape rejection, linear acquire/transfer/consume ledgers, device address-space/transfer/synchronization/lifetime checks, audited raw-memory wrappers, and agreement of retained checks with exact proof-elision records; atomics with target memory order/scope/alignment, structured task parent or explicit lifecycle owner, cancellation cleanup and failure propagation, actor/channel schemas with ordering/backpressure/transfer policy; FFI symbol/loading policy, ABI/layout conformance, null/handle/lifetime/ownership/error adapters and callbacks re-entering capability/taint/thread-affinity/scheduler checks. Reject mismatched providers, races, orphan tasks, unsupported atomics, schemaless messages, raw extern safe calls and invalid callback entry. Dependencies: ownership and Legality supply compile-time facts, Lower supplies target layouts, Auth supplies grants, and distributed execution supplies replay policy; runtime debug checks cannot substitute for compile-time safety. P4/P5: host-object/native FFI records bind runtime/version/symbol, Gravity and foreign types, rooting/ownership/lifetime, nullability, failure mapping, affinity, ABI, effects/grants and safe wrappers. Insufficient host metadata permits opaque provider-only handles, not unrestricted manipulation; raw native imports are not directly safe-callable. Exercise positive boundaries and missing metadata, ungranted call, invalid lifetime and untranslated failure rejection. Residual criterion runtime/foreign-symbol-resolution: Resolve a declared foreign symbol and dynamically load an admitted library/module only under package/deployment policy, the named provider/library/version identity and required effects/grants. Emit the binding, symbol-resolution and generated-adapter records tied to target ABI, calling convention, layout/alignment and source/unsafe audit. Positive fixtures resolve the admitted identity through its safe wrapper/provider; negative fixtures reject wrong/missing symbols, mismatched ABI/layout/provider identity and ungranted or policy-denied dynamic loading. Resolution/loading does not bypass nullability, lifetime/ownership, callback affinity/taint or foreign error conversion contracts. Preserve the delivered split between resolution and loading as two criteria within this same task, without accepting an alias or retiring their history. Foundation requirement gravity/interop-boundary-manifest: Produce and consume the typed foreign boundary manifest with applicable ABI/layout, ownership/transfer/lifetime, null/error/callback/thread, host/schema/provider, effects/grants and provenance obligations; demonstrate a conforming boundary invocation. Refusals: Reject a missing applicable obligation, incompatible ABI/schema/provider, invalid ownership transfer or absent authority; a declaration-only check does not prove actual conversion or callback execution. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): schema - Versioned source schema, generated validators/codecs and parity artifacts; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products. Foundation requirement gravity/interop-is-not-host-semantics: Normalize an admitted foreign value/failure/callback through its declared typed and audited Gravity boundary while preserving Gravity errors, source identity, effects and capability requirements. Refusals: Reject a host null, exception, reflection/loading convention or object-identity assumption leaking into portable Gravity semantics; keep actual adaptation separate from manifest publication. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-runtimebuildeditor-consumers-without-rule-drift - Actual runtime/compiler/tool structured diagnostics with stable owning codes and provenance. Criterion profile-gap/hosted/typed-object-boundary (Open): Input: Host object boundary with runtime/version, symbol/class/module/member, Gravity/host type, rooting/ownership/lifetime, exception translation, affinity, effects/grants and source-map support. Accept: Emit and validate typed schema/protocol/foreign-handle boundaries before manipulation; insufficient metadata yields opaque values operated only through declared provider APIs. Reject: Untyped host object use, missing lifecycle/affinity/grant metadata and unnormalized host failures crossing into Gravity. Required outputs: Host interop/object/runtime dependency and deployment-capability manifests, typed-versus-opaque boundary 