  "- [ ] `evolution/change-review` Produce and validate the accountable change lifecycle\n\nStatus: Open\n\nSource requirement: `governance/change-review`\n\nRequired outputs: Owned change record with affected documents, surfaces, state and complete decision history Compatibility, safety/security, profile, artifact, bootstrap and conformance impact dossier Accepted-for-implementation, implemented and stabilized transitions with distinct evidence and release-note links\n\nClosing evidence: An owned nontrivial change passes sketch/draft/RFC/prototype/review/accepted/implemented/stabilized states only with each applicable GOV1/GOV6 gate; rejected/removed records remain durable history. Stable changes carry GOV2 comparison/migration; safety/profile/artifact/bootstrap changes carry actual negative fixtures, matrix/schema/provenance/equivalence inputs. Release provenance follows change ID through affected specs, implementation, conformance and user-visible notes; implementation acceptance is a separate recorded decision. Actual complete accepted artifact and consumer result for the named source contract, with input/source/policy/tool identity. Historical stage0 records or a passing schema alone do not implement these outcomes. Stable source-language revision adoption is a conditional instance of this same change-decision producer, with the existing semantic maintainers supplying the following exact evidence. For stable source-language contract revisions only, produce a scoped adoption decision after consuming the exact required source changes, compatibility/safety reviews and affected conformance outputs. This task does not gate ordinary semantic development or confer release/implementation acceptance. Source obligation `language/concurrency/review-semantic-change`: Update safety and runtime conformance consumers when concurrency semantics change. Accept: For an admitted concurrency-semantic revision, identify effects on memory/data-race safety, runtime, GPU/hardware lowering, workflow replay, AI plans and performance; update the affected safety and runtime conformance suites. Reject: Deny stable adoption when an affected safety/runtime suite or consumer disposition is missing, stale or failing. Required outputs: Revision-bound impact matrix, updated positive/negative safety/runtime fixtures and scoped adoption decision. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/core/version-semantic-change`: Update the affected contracts, schemas and conformance consumers before admitting a changed core semantic rule. Accept: Before stable adoption of a new core form or changed order/truthiness/mutation/error rule, update affected syntax, type, effect, safety, compiler, backend, runtime, test and documentation artifacts. Reject: Deny adoption with an omitted consumer, stale schema/fixture or unqualified host/backend semantic substitution. Required outputs: Exact old/new L2 rule, consumer/schema change matrix, positive/negative conformance outputs and scoped admission receipt. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core5-integrate-semantic-analyses, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/finish-managednative-execution-startup-panic-and-cleanup; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/effects/register-stable-semantic-extension`: Register a new effect label or handler/resume/replay semantic form through governance before stable use, updating all affected policy, runtime and conformance consumers. Accept: Register a new effect label, handler form, resume mode or replay mode before stable use, defining profile legality, capability requirements, ordering, diagnostics and artifact representation. Update affected profiles, capability/package/build policy, runtime, compiler, AI/workflow and conformance consumers. Reject: Deny stable use of an unregistered label/form/mode or a change missing any affected policy/consumer/fixture disposition. Required outputs: Versioned effect/handler registry entry, compatibility/consumer matrix, legal/illegal fixtures and stable-use decision. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/errors/review-representation-change`: Obtain compatibility review before changing a stable API's error representation, updating affected semantic/runtime/interop consumers. Accept: Obtain compatibility review before a stable API error-representation change; update affected core, types/effects, profiles, runtimes, FFI, workflows, AI, library, diagnostics and test consumers. Reject: Deny stable adoption without the required compatibility disposition or affected consumer updates. Required outputs: Old/new error representation, compatibility receipt, consumer migration/fixture results and adoption decision. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/finish-managednative-execution-startup-panic-and-cleanup; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/macro/version-semantics-change`: Update the affected syntax schemas, diagnostic/tooling consumers, macro safety fixtures and bootstrap equivalence checks when macro semantics change. Accept: For a macro-semantic revision, update syntax-object schema, macro fixtures, generated-origin diagnostics, formatter/LSP, compiler bootstrapping, macro safety and self-hosting equivalence consumers. Reject: Deny stable adoption when an affected schema/fixture/consumer remains stale or equivalence changes lack scoped review. Required outputs: Exact macro revision, consumer/schema/equivalence impact matrix, positive/negative fixtures and adoption receipt. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from expand/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/expand5-integrate-generated-programs, syntax/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/syntax1-construct-canonical-syntax, core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core5-integrate-semantic-analyses; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/memory/review-safety-change`: Obtain safety review and update downstream fixtures before weakening a safe memory guarantee. Accept: Before adopting a weakened safe-memory guarantee, obtain safety review and update affected type/effect/safety/profile/optimizer/backend/runtime/FFI/library/conformance fixtures. Reject: Deny stable adoption without safety review or with a missing downstream guarantee/fixture disposition. Required outputs: Old/new safety guarantee, independent safety-review receipt, downstream positive/negative fixture matrix and adoption decision. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/module/review-compatibility-change`: Update namespace/module conformance and obtain package compatibility review for a changed namespace or module rule. Accept: For a namespace/module-rule change, update macro/type/effect/package-resolution/artifact-identity/LSP/docs/bootstrap-order consumers and conformance fixtures; obtain package compatibility review. Reject: Deny stable adoption with missing package compatibility review, inconsistent module identity or stale affected fixtures. Required outputs: Versioned namespace/module contract, consumer/fixture matrix, package compatibility receipt and adoption decision. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from expand/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/expand5-integrate-generated-programs, build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/pattern/version-pattern-change`: Update conformance consumers for every affected pattern family when pattern semantics change. Accept: For a pattern-semantic change, update conformance for each affected pattern family and its core lowering, narrowing, effects, ownership, schema, workflow/AI branching, formal and backend consumers. Reject: Deny stable adoption when an affected pattern family or required consumer lacks a current conformance disposition. Required outputs: Pattern-family/consumer impact matrix, accepted/rejected match fixtures and scoped adoption receipt. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core5-integrate-semantic-analyses, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/protocol/review-stable-change`: Obtain compatibility and conformance review before changing a stable protocol or dispatch semantic contract. Accept: Before a stable protocol/dispatch-semantic revision, obtain compatibility and conformance review across affected types/effects, performance, backend ABI, host interop, library, AI tools and formal consumers. Reject: Deny stable adoption without review or with stale method/dispatch/ABI/conformance consumers. Required outputs: Old/new protocol/dispatch contract, compatibility and conformance receipts, consumer fixtures and adoption decision. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/syntax/change-adoption-fixtures`: Require read, print, format, macro-expansion and diagnostic fixtures before adopting an added or changed surface syntax contract. Accept: Before adopting added/changed surface syntax, update affected reader/syntax/macro/formatter/linter/LSP/diagnostic/test/bootstrap consumers and supply read, print, format, macro-expansion and diagnostic fixtures. Reject: Deny stable syntax adoption if any required fixture family or affected consumer disposition is missing or failing. Required outputs: Old/new syntax rule, five fixture-family results, consumer change matrix and scoped adoption receipt. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from syntax/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/syntax1-construct-canonical-syntax, expand/current-